      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T01:45:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I intentionally didn\u0027t change this one:\n- GetActivePageObjectCount() is O(n) to get the count, whereas GetPageObjectCount() is O(1)\n- This method isn\u0027t interested in an exact count anyway; it only wants to know if it is exactly 1 or not.\n\nSo all the work for getting the particular number of objects is overkill.  It is cheaper to use GetPageObjectCount() as before, plus a local explicit check for IsActive() instead.\n\nAdded a comment to that regard.",
      "parentUuid": "f3cf8d7a_45d2cb40",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "7c6876839759c99c5457731e88fdc2e42704bf7e",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3ab10f91_599fc0c1",
        "filename": "core/fpdfapi/page/cpdf_form.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 124,
      "author": {
        "id": 5045
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T01:51:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What if the object count is 2, with 1 active and 1 not active?\n\nIf you agree this is a potential issue that the current code does not handle correctly, then can you add a TODO for making a pass at this later?",
      "parentUuid": "5a5c174f_f9d34ebe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "7c6876839759c99c5457731e88fdc2e42704bf7e",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d53cc71d_5b80469c",
        "filename": "core/fpdfapi/page/cpdf_form.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 124,
      "author": {
        "id": 7704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T02:05:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This method is rather explicitly named:  `GetBitmapAndMatrixFromSoleImageOfForm()`.  If the form has 2 objects, then wouldn\u0027t it already have violated what this method is expecting for \"sole image of form\"?\n\nI.e., the fact that one of those two might be inactive doesn\u0027t seem relative, it already has violated the \"sole\" part by there being more than one page object.",
      "parentUuid": "3ab10f91_599fc0c1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "7c6876839759c99c5457731e88fdc2e42704bf7e",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5b625b24_d61e4202",
        "filename": "core/fpdfapi/page/cpdf_form.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 124,
      "author": {
        "id": 5045
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T02:15:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To be clear, my interpretation of the existing code, prior to this CL, is that the following conditions must all be true for this to return the image:\n- There is 1 and only 1 page object.\n- That object is an image.\n\nThat does not mean the form cannot have 2 objects inside. It just means those with 2 objects inside gets rejected.\n\nWith the existing code, there is no concept of \"active\", so all page objects are active by default. Thus having 2 page object means failing the conditions above.\n\nWith this CL, now comes the \"active\" concept. If there are 2 objects inside, with only 1 active, wouldn\u0027t this method need to ignore the inactive object and treat this case as though there is only 1?",
      "parentUuid": "d53cc71d_5b80469c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "7c6876839759c99c5457731e88fdc2e42704bf7e",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0e238d42_fbc46544",
        "filename": "core/fpdfapi/page/cpdf_form.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 124,
      "author": {
        "id": 5045
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T02:28:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Another way to think about this is that this new API is an optimization. Without it, a PDFium embedder could instead take all N page objects out of page, insert an object, and then put the N page objects back in. But that\u0027s a lot of shuffling and this new API lets the PDFium embedder avoid that work, by simply treating the page object as though it is not there.\n\nSo if there are 2 objects, and only 1 is active, then shouldn\u0027t the inactive object be treated as though it is not there? Thus making the object count 1, right?\n\nBTW, testing/corpus/pdfium/bug_651304.pdf is an example where the page object count is 2. That can be the basis for a test case in the future to test this out with FPDFPageObj_SetIsActive().",
      "parentUuid": "5b625b24_d61e4202",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "7c6876839759c99c5457731e88fdc2e42704bf7e",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6e6b16b4_bdc1ca29",
        "filename": "core/fpdfapi/page/cpdf_form.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 124,
      "author": {
        "id": 7704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-11-07T02:32:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If there are 2 objects inside the form, with only 1 active, then is that one active object the sole object of the form?\n\nWDYT about giving this method a slight rename?  If this was changed to `GetBitmapAndMatrixFromSoleActiveImageOfForm()`, then it would be clear that this should be using GetActivePageObjectCount(), and callers could also be clear about the expectations here.",
      "parentUuid": "5b625b24_d61e4202",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 124,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 124,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "7c6876839759c99c5457731e88fdc2e42704bf7e",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
